      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The introduction of minimally invasive surgery (MIS) has led to new clinical pathways for total knee arthroplasty (TKA). MIS TKA outcomes are affected by multiple factors--the surgery itself; preoperative planning and medical management; preoperative patient education; preemptive perioperative and postoperative analgesia; mode of anesthesia; optimal rehabilitation; and enlightened home care and social services-and therefore an integrated team approach to patient and surgery is required."},
